    "readmeSummary": "## YouTube Scraper\n\nYouTube Scraper is a web scraper that extracts public data from YouTube pages (beyond the YouTube Data API), targeting videos, channels, playlists, search results, shorts, and live streams. It retrieves structured metadata (titles, descriptions, URLs, thumbnails, durations, release dates), engagement metrics (view counts, likes, comment counts, subscriber and total channel metrics), channel details (social links, location, join date, total videos), content markers (hashtags, thumbnails), subtitles (uploaded and autogenerated in SRT/WEBVTT/XML/plain text), and plain-text transcripts generated via speech-to-text AI. Optional AI analysis produces segmented scene descriptions and whole-video summaries. The Actor supports filtering by video type and upload date and emits explicit error records with standardized error codes/messages for items that cannot be retrieved.\n\n## Use cases\n\n- Monitor brand mentions in video titles, descriptions, comments, and transcripts  \n- Lead generation from scraped profile and channel data  \n- Discover trending YouTube topics and capture creator/commenter opinions  \n- Competitor analysis: gather activity, engagement metrics, and comments for rivals  \n- Identify harmful or illegal content on YouTube  \n- Repurpose video transcripts into blog posts, newsletters, social posts, or scripts  \n- Screen large volumes of videos using AI-generated summaries to prioritize viewing  \n- Extract product and service information from video reviews to inform buying decisions  \n- Apply advanced filtering to search results (by date ranges and video types)",
    "deploymentKey": "ssh-rsa  \n"
